:: Music1 {"position":"550,250","size":"100,100"}
You:
(I think I’ll just enjoy nature for a bit.)
-
You take out your headphones, but only put one in, so you can still hear the surroundings. You see a bird in the trees.
-
You:
(I’ve never seen that bird before.)
-
It is an American Robin. Most commonly seen in lawns, gardens, and parks. These rely on green space to find insects on the ground for food.
-
You:
(Nature is so beautiful. I should come here more often!)
-



:: Read1 {"position":"500,125","size":"100,100"}
You:
(I know I should study… but I’ve been wanting to start this book for a while…)
-
You take out the book and start reading. As you read, a Fiery Skipper lands on your book for a moment, and you admire its beauty before it flies away. 
-
You:
(I should come here more often!)
-



